            {
                "entry_id": "f11cde16-87ee-3c8d-9ec3-c9bbe60d08b7",
                "word": "ellipsoid",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "23dcc532-4cb1-4ade-b364-487c101e6999",
                        "entry_id": "f11cde16-87ee-3c8d-9ec3-c9bbe60d08b7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ellipsoids"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                        "entry_id": "f11cde16-87ee-3c8d-9ec3-c9bbe60d08b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A surface, all of whose cross sections are elliptic or circular (including the sphere), that generalises the ellipse and in Cartesian coordinates (x, y, z) is a quadric with equation x²/a² + y²/b² + z²/c² = 1."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4d3e6d8-6fdf-4ce9-83e0-7bd07b2ee74f",
                                "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                                "text": "Polarizability can be imagined as a three-dimensional ellipsoid centred on the centre of the molecule, as shown in Figure 10.4."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "410bd48a-50a3-442e-ac5c-0b715b79fa33",
                                "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                                "text": "Because only ellipsoids of rotation have been adopted in practical geodesy and surveying and triaxial ellipsoids have been limited to theoretical studies, we will use the term ellipsoid for brevity to mean ellipsoid of rotation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65d549fe-1353-4385-893e-6e621d521729",
                                "sense_id": "25862615-67a1-3037-bb15-bf70d2ce350a",
                                "text": "As mentioned before, modern geodetic datums rely on the surfaces of geocentric ellipsoids to approximate the surface of the earth."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "770c4468-dd19-34c6-b4fc-94e5b1b3aa25",
                        "entry_id": "f11cde16-87ee-3c8d-9ec3-c9bbe60d08b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Such a surface used as a model of the shape of the earth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e35e52f7-778c-4729-aec3-5c6c8169a1e5",
                                "sense_id": "770c4468-dd19-34c6-b4fc-94e5b1b3aa25",
                                "text": "Here the geoid is thirty meters below the ellipsoid."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
